{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sunburst"},{"type":"text","value":" partitions a flat hierarchy into nested angular sectors. It runs\ninside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"polar"},{"type":"text","value":", so ring radii resolve from the final polar layout without\napplication-owned partition rows or D3 arc generators."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { sunburst } from '@tanstack/charts/hierarchy/sunburst'\nimport { polar } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\n\nconst chart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    polar({\n      startAngle: Math.PI / 2,\n      endAngle: Math.PI / 2 - Math.PI * 2,\n      marks: [\n        sunburst(rows, {\n          path: 'name',\n          delimiter: '.',\n          value: 'size',\n          rootId: '/flare/analytics',\n          visibleDepth: 2,\n          innerRadius: ({ radius }) => radius * 0.14,\n          ringPadding: 2,\n          color: 'branchId',\n          stroke: '#fff',\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        angle: null,\n        radius: null,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The exact "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/hierarchy/sunburst"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath keeps hierarchy\nconstruction and partitioning out of root, universal, ordinary polar, and\nradial-bar consumers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hierarchy-input","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hierarchy input"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path input constructs parent-child relationships from a string channel:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sunburst(rows, {\n  path: 'name',\n  delimiter: '.',\n  value: 'size',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit parent references use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodeId"},{"type":"text","value":" because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" identifies the mark:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sunburst(rows, {\n  id: 'package-sunburst',\n  nodeId: 'id',\n  parentId: 'parentId',\n  value: 'size',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path input may omit ancestors. Those structural nodes have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data: null"},{"type":"text","value":" and\nempty direct lineage. Duplicate identities, invalid parents, multiple roots,\nand cycles throw before rendering. Source child order is preserved unless\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sort"},{"type":"text","value":" is supplied."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path-mode node IDs use the shared hierarchy contract's canonical slash form,\nindependent of the authored delimiter. The original row and path remain on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":"; use them when presentation must preserve source spelling. Path-mode\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" is the terminal path segment. Explicit-parent IDs are opaque, so their\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" is the complete authored ID even when it contains a slash."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstPathOptions<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstParentOptions<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" form the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstOptions<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" union."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path mode only"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full hierarchy path"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delimiter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One-character path separator"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodeId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parent mode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit node identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TDatum, string?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parent mode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit parent identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nonnegative contribution aggregated through parents"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sort"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstNodeComparator<TDatum>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source order"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sibling comparator over immutable node values"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rootId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hierarchy root"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node whose children form the first rendered ring"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visibleDepth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All depths"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maximum descendant rings below the active root"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"innerRadius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PolarLength"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive inner edge of the first rendered ring"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outerRadius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PolarLength"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layout radius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive outer edge of the last rendered ring"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ringPadding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixed CSS-pixel gap between hierarchy depths"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark identity and optional class"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Geometry and interaction group"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value sent to the chart color scale"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Color / none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-sector paint"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sector presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sector stroke dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whole-sector opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkMotionOptions<SunburstNode<TDatum>>['motion']"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-node motion policy"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nullish values contribute zero. Other values must be finite and nonnegative.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ringPadding"},{"type":"text","value":" is a nonnegative pixel value. If padding consumes the available\nradial span, the mark omits sectors instead of emitting inverted rings."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-partition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive partition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The enclosing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"polar"},{"type":"text","value":" mark owns the angular sweep and final center. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sunburst"},{"type":"text","value":"\nallocates each node's angle from its aggregate value and divides the resolved\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"innerRadius"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outerRadius"},{"type":"text","value":" span into equal depth rings. The radius options\naccept pixel lengths or responsive callbacks through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PolarLength"},{"type":"text","value":". Both\nresolved radii must be finite and nonnegative; their order controls the ring\ndirection."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ringPadding"},{"type":"text","value":" remains a fixed pixel gap as the chart resizes. It does not\nchange the hierarchy values or angular allocation. Sectors replay the shared\nrenderer-neutral D3 path commands into a sampled interaction polygon, so\nrounded, reversed, and complete sectors retain paint-faithful focus geometry."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"drill-down-and-motion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drill-down and motion"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rootId"},{"type":"text","value":" makes an existing hierarchy node the structural root without changing\nits canonical ID or rebuilding source rows. Its children become depth one, and\nthe root itself is not painted. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visibleDepth"},{"type":"text","value":" is relative to that root; hidden\ndescendants still contribute to aggregate values and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"internal"},{"type":"text","value":" metadata."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = (rootId: string) =>\n  defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      polar({\n        marks: [\n          sunburst(rows, {\n            id: 'package-sunburst',\n            path: 'name',\n            delimiter: '.',\n            value: 'size',\n            rootId,\n            visibleDepth: 2,\n          }),\n        ],\n        scales: {\n          angle: null,\n          radius: null,\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: null,\n      y: null,\n    },\n    motion: {\n      transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 720, easing: 'ease-in-out' },\n    },\n  })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rebuild the definition when application navigation changes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rootId"},{"type":"text","value":", and mount\nit with the optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" renderer. Retained descendants keep their node\nkeys. Sunburst motion interpolates each sector's angles and radii, then\nregenerates a valid concentric arc around the fixed polar center every frame.\nNewly revealed descendants unfold from their nearest disappearing ancestor\nsector. During drill-up, removed descendants collapse into their nearest\nappearing ancestor. Nodes without an overlapping lineage use the normal enter\nor exit opacity transition. The renderer snaps these updates when the user\nrequests reduced motion."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In path mode, pass the canonical slash ID such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/flare/analytics"},{"type":"text","value":", not the\nauthored delimiter spelling. Explicit-parent IDs remain opaque."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"nodes-and-lineage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nodes and lineage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The root is structural and is not painted. Every rendered sector carries one\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstNode<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" with:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentId"},{"type":"text","value":", and root-to-parent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ancestorIds"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"depth"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"internal"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external"},{"type":"text","value":" metadata;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"aggregate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"branchId"},{"type":"text","value":", equal to the first node below the root for that branch;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the direct authored "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" row, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" for an imputed node; and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"direct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceIndexes"},{"type":"text","value":" lineage."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"branchId"},{"type":"text","value":" is useful for inherited branch color: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color: 'branchId'"},{"type":"text","value":" gives a\ntop-level branch and all its descendants one color without preparing a color\nfield. Paint, motion, and sort callbacks receive the same immutable node\nvalues."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The exact entry exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sunburst"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstNode"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstNodeComparator"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstPathOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstParentOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SunburstOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./polar.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Polar Marks"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for angular sweeps and responsive\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PolarLength"},{"type":"text","value":" values."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"hierarchy-input","text":"Hierarchy input","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"responsive-partition","text":"Responsive partition","level":2},{"id":"drill-down-and-motion","text":"Drill-down and motion","level":2},{"id":"nodes-and-lineage","text":"Nodes and lineage","level":2},{"id":"types","text":"Types","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`sunburst` partitions a flat hierarchy into nested angular sectors. It runs\ninside `polar`, so ring radii resolve from the final polar layout without\napplication-owned partition rows or D3 arc generators.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { sunburst } from '@tanstack/charts/hierarchy/sunburst'\nimport { polar } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\n\nconst chart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    polar({\n      startAngle: Math.PI / 2,\n      endAngle: Math.PI / 2 - Math.PI * 2,\n      marks: [\n        sunburst(rows, {\n          path: 'name',\n          delimiter: '.',\n          value: 'size',\n          rootId: '/flare/analytics',\n          visibleDepth: 2,\n          innerRadius: ({ radius }) => radius * 0.14,\n          ringPadding: 2,\n          color: 'branchId',\n          stroke: '#fff',\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        angle: null,\n        radius: null,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe exact `@tanstack/charts/hierarchy/sunburst` subpath keeps hierarchy\nconstruction and partitioning out of root, universal, ordinary polar, and\nradial-bar consumers.\n\n## Hierarchy input\n\nPath input constructs parent-child relationships from a string channel:\n\n```ts\nsunburst(rows, {\n  path: 'name',\n  delimiter: '.',\n  value: 'size',\n})\n```\n\nExplicit parent references use `nodeId` because `id` identifies the mark:\n\n```ts\nsunburst(rows, {\n  id: 'package-sunburst',\n  nodeId: 'id',\n  parentId: 'parentId',\n  value: 'size',\n})\n```\n\nPath input may omit ancestors. Those structural nodes have `data: null` and\nempty direct lineage. Duplicate identities, invalid parents, multiple roots,\nand cycles throw before rendering. Source child order is preserved unless\n`sort` is supplied.\n\nPath-mode node IDs use the shared hierarchy contract's canonical slash form,\nindependent of the authored delimiter. The original row and path remain on\n`data`; use them when presentation must preserve source spelling. Path-mode\n`name` is the terminal path segment. Explicit-parent IDs are opaque, so their\n`name` is the complete authored ID even when it contains a slash.\n\n## Options\n\n`SunburstPathOptions<TDatum>` and `SunburstParentOptions<TDatum>` form the\n`SunburstOptions<TDatum>` union.\n\n| Option                                        | Type                                                     | Default        | Meaning                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `path`                                        | `TransformValue<TDatum, string>`                         | Path mode only | Full hierarchy path                                 |\n| `delimiter`                                   | `string`                                                 | `/`            | One-character path separator                        |\n| `nodeId`                                      | `TransformValue<TDatum, string>`                         | Parent mode    | Explicit node identity                              |\n| `parentId`                                    | `TransformValue<TDatum, string?>`                        | Parent mode    | Explicit parent identity                            |\n| `value`                                       | `TransformValue<TDatum, number?>`                        | Required       | Nonnegative contribution aggregated through parents |\n| `sort`                                        | `SunburstNodeComparator<TDatum>`                         | Source order   | Sibling comparator over immutable node values       |\n| `rootId`                                      | `string`                                                 | Hierarchy root | Node whose children form the first rendered ring    |\n| `visibleDepth`                                | `number`                                                 | All depths     | Maximum descendant rings below the active root      |\n| `innerRadius`                                 | `PolarLength`                                            | `0`            | Responsive inner edge of the first rendered ring    |\n| `outerRadius`                                 | `PolarLength`                                            | Layout radius  | Responsive outer edge of the last rendered ring     |\n| `ringPadding`                                 | `number`                                                 | `0`            | Fixed CSS-pixel gap between hierarchy depths        |\n| `id`, `className`                             | `string`                                                 | Derived        | Stable mark identity and optional class             |\n| `z`                                           | `Channel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, ChartKey?>`               | No group       | Geometry and interaction group                      |\n| `color`                                       | `Channel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, ChartKey?>`               | `z`            | Value sent to the chart color scale                 |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                              | `VisualChannel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, string>`            | Color / none   | Per-sector paint                                    |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, `strokeWidth` | `number`                                                 | Renderer value | Sector presentation                                 |\n| `strokeDasharray`                             | `string`                                                 | None           | Sector stroke dash pattern                          |\n| `opacity`                                     | `number`                                                 | Renderer value | Whole-sector opacity                                |\n| `motion`                                      | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<SunburstNode<TDatum>>['motion']` | None           | Per-node motion policy                              |\n\nNullish values contribute zero. Other values must be finite and nonnegative.\n`ringPadding` is a nonnegative pixel value. If padding consumes the available\nradial span, the mark omits sectors instead of emitting inverted rings.\n\n## Responsive partition\n\nThe enclosing `polar` mark owns the angular sweep and final center. `sunburst`\nallocates each node's angle from its aggregate value and divides the resolved\n`innerRadius` to `outerRadius` span into equal depth rings. The radius options\naccept pixel lengths or responsive callbacks through `PolarLength`. Both\nresolved radii must be finite and nonnegative; their order controls the ring\ndirection.\n\n`ringPadding` remains a fixed pixel gap as the chart resizes. It does not\nchange the hierarchy values or angular allocation. Sectors replay the shared\nrenderer-neutral D3 path commands into a sampled interaction polygon, so\nrounded, reversed, and complete sectors retain paint-faithful focus geometry.\n\n## Drill-down and motion\n\n`rootId` makes an existing hierarchy node the structural root without changing\nits canonical ID or rebuilding source rows. Its children become depth one, and\nthe root itself is not painted. `visibleDepth` is relative to that root; hidden\ndescendants still contribute to aggregate values and `internal` metadata.\n\n```ts\nconst definition = (rootId: string) =>\n  defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      polar({\n        marks: [\n          sunburst(rows, {\n            id: 'package-sunburst',\n            path: 'name',\n            delimiter: '.',\n            value: 'size',\n            rootId,\n            visibleDepth: 2,\n          }),\n        ],\n        scales: {\n          angle: null,\n          radius: null,\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: null,\n      y: null,\n    },\n    motion: {\n      transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 720, easing: 'ease-in-out' },\n    },\n  })\n```\n\nRebuild the definition when application navigation changes `rootId`, and mount\nit with the optional `motion()` renderer. Retained descendants keep their node\nkeys. Sunburst motion interpolates each sector's angles and radii, then\nregenerates a valid concentric arc around the fixed polar center every frame.\nNewly revealed descendants unfold from their nearest disappearing ancestor\nsector. During drill-up, removed descendants collapse into their nearest\nappearing ancestor. Nodes without an overlapping lineage use the normal enter\nor exit opacity transition. The renderer snaps these updates when the user\nrequests reduced motion.\n\nIn path mode, pass the canonical slash ID such as `/flare/analytics`, not the\nauthored delimiter spelling. Explicit-parent IDs remain opaque.\n\n## Nodes and lineage\n\nThe root is structural and is not painted. Every rendered sector carries one\n`SunburstNode<TDatum>` with:\n\n- stable `id`, `parentId`, and root-to-parent `ancestorIds`;\n- `name`, `depth`, `height`, and `internal` / `external` metadata;\n- aggregate `value`;\n- `branchId`, equal to the first node below the root for that branch;\n- the direct authored `data` row, or `null` for an imputed node; and\n- direct `source` and `sourceIndexes` lineage.\n\n`branchId` is useful for inherited branch color: `color: 'branchId'` gives a\ntop-level branch and all its descendants one color without preparing a color\nfield. Paint, motion, and sort callbacks receive the same immutable node\nvalues.\n\n## Types\n\nThe exact entry exports `sunburst`, `SunburstNode`,\n`SunburstNodeComparator`, `SunburstPathOptions`, `SunburstParentOptions`, and\n`SunburstOptions`.\n\nSee [Polar Marks](./polar.md) for angular sweeps and responsive\n`PolarLength` values.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Sunburst Mark\ndescription: Reference for flat hierarchy input, responsive radial partitioning, node lineage, branch color, and the optional sunburst import.\n---\n\n`sunburst` partitions a flat hierarchy into nested angular sectors. It runs\ninside `polar`, so ring radii resolve from the final polar layout without\napplication-owned partition rows or D3 arc generators.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { sunburst } from '@tanstack/charts/hierarchy/sunburst'\nimport { polar } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\n\nconst chart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    polar({\n      startAngle: Math.PI / 2,\n      endAngle: Math.PI / 2 - Math.PI * 2,\n      marks: [\n        sunburst(rows, {\n          path: 'name',\n          delimiter: '.',\n          value: 'size',\n          rootId: '/flare/analytics',\n          visibleDepth: 2,\n          innerRadius: ({ radius }) => radius * 0.14,\n          ringPadding: 2,\n          color: 'branchId',\n          stroke: '#fff',\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        angle: null,\n        radius: null,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe exact `@tanstack/charts/hierarchy/sunburst` subpath keeps hierarchy\nconstruction and partitioning out of root, universal, ordinary polar, and\nradial-bar consumers.\n\n## Hierarchy input\n\nPath input constructs parent-child relationships from a string channel:\n\n```ts\nsunburst(rows, {\n  path: 'name',\n  delimiter: '.',\n  value: 'size',\n})\n```\n\nExplicit parent references use `nodeId` because `id` identifies the mark:\n\n```ts\nsunburst(rows, {\n  id: 'package-sunburst',\n  nodeId: 'id',\n  parentId: 'parentId',\n  value: 'size',\n})\n```\n\nPath input may omit ancestors. Those structural nodes have `data: null` and\nempty direct lineage. Duplicate identities, invalid parents, multiple roots,\nand cycles throw before rendering. Source child order is preserved unless\n`sort` is supplied.\n\nPath-mode node IDs use the shared hierarchy contract's canonical slash form,\nindependent of the authored delimiter. The original row and path remain on\n`data`; use them when presentation must preserve source spelling. Path-mode\n`name` is the terminal path segment. Explicit-parent IDs are opaque, so their\n`name` is the complete authored ID even when it contains a slash.\n\n## Options\n\n`SunburstPathOptions<TDatum>` and `SunburstParentOptions<TDatum>` form the\n`SunburstOptions<TDatum>` union.\n\n| Option                                        | Type                                                     | Default        | Meaning                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `path`                                        | `TransformValue<TDatum, string>`                         | Path mode only | Full hierarchy path                                 |\n| `delimiter`                                   | `string`                                                 | `/`            | One-character path separator                        |\n| `nodeId`                                      | `TransformValue<TDatum, string>`                         | Parent mode    | Explicit node identity                              |\n| `parentId`                                    | `TransformValue<TDatum, string?>`                        | Parent mode    | Explicit parent identity                            |\n| `value`                                       | `TransformValue<TDatum, number?>`                        | Required       | Nonnegative contribution aggregated through parents |\n| `sort`                                        | `SunburstNodeComparator<TDatum>`                         | Source order   | Sibling comparator over immutable node values       |\n| `rootId`                                      | `string`                                                 | Hierarchy root | Node whose children form the first rendered ring    |\n| `visibleDepth`                                | `number`                                                 | All depths     | Maximum descendant rings below the active root      |\n| `innerRadius`                                 | `PolarLength`                                            | `0`            | Responsive inner edge of the first rendered ring    |\n| `outerRadius`                                 | `PolarLength`                                            | Layout radius  | Responsive outer edge of the last rendered ring     |\n| `ringPadding`                                 | `number`                                                 | `0`            | Fixed CSS-pixel gap between hierarchy depths        |\n| `id`, `className`                             | `string`                                                 | Derived        | Stable mark identity and optional class             |\n| `z`                                           | `Channel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, ChartKey?>`               | No group       | Geometry and interaction group                      |\n| `color`                                       | `Channel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, ChartKey?>`               | `z`            | Value sent to the chart color scale                 |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                              | `VisualChannel<SunburstNode<TDatum>, string>`            | Color / none   | Per-sector paint                                    |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, `strokeWidth` | `number`                                                 | Renderer value | Sector presentation                                 |\n| `strokeDasharray`                             | `string`                                                 | None           | Sector stroke dash pattern                          |\n| `opacity`                                     | `number`                                                 | Renderer value | Whole-sector opacity                                |\n| `motion`                                      | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<SunburstNode<TDatum>>['motion']` | None           | Per-node motion policy                              |\n\nNullish values contribute zero. Other values must be finite and nonnegative.\n`ringPadding` is a nonnegative pixel value. If padding consumes the available\nradial span, the mark omits sectors instead of emitting inverted rings.\n\n## Responsive partition\n\nThe enclosing `polar` mark owns the angular sweep and final center. `sunburst`\nallocates each node's angle from its aggregate value and divides the resolved\n`innerRadius` to `outerRadius` span into equal depth rings. The radius options\naccept pixel lengths or responsive callbacks through `PolarLength`. Both\nresolved radii must be finite and nonnegative; their order controls the ring\ndirection.\n\n`ringPadding` remains a fixed pixel gap as the chart resizes. It does not\nchange the hierarchy values or angular allocation. Sectors replay the shared\nrenderer-neutral D3 path commands into a sampled interaction polygon, so\nrounded, reversed, and complete sectors retain paint-faithful focus geometry.\n\n## Drill-down and motion\n\n`rootId` makes an existing hierarchy node the structural root without changing\nits canonical ID or rebuilding source rows. Its children become depth one, and\nthe root itself is not painted. `visibleDepth` is relative to that root; hidden\ndescendants still contribute to aggregate values and `internal` metadata.\n\n```ts\nconst definition = (rootId: string) =>\n  defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      polar({\n        marks: [\n          sunburst(rows, {\n            id: 'package-sunburst',\n            path: 'name',\n            delimiter: '.',\n            value: 'size',\n            rootId,\n            visibleDepth: 2,\n          }),\n        ],\n        scales: {\n          angle: null,\n          radius: null,\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: null,\n      y: null,\n    },\n    motion: {\n      transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 720, easing: 'ease-in-out' },\n    },\n  })\n```\n\nRebuild the definition when application navigation changes `rootId`, and mount\nit with the optional `motion()` renderer. Retained descendants keep their node\nkeys. Sunburst motion interpolates each sector's angles and radii, then\nregenerates a valid concentric arc around the fixed polar center every frame.\nNewly revealed descendants unfold from their nearest disappearing ancestor\nsector. During drill-up, removed descendants collapse into their nearest\nappearing ancestor. Nodes without an overlapping lineage use the normal enter\nor exit opacity transition. The renderer snaps these updates when the user\nrequests reduced motion.\n\nIn path mode, pass the canonical slash ID such as `/flare/analytics`, not the\nauthored delimiter spelling. Explicit-parent IDs remain opaque.\n\n## Nodes and lineage\n\nThe root is structural and is not painted. Every rendered sector carries one\n`SunburstNode<TDatum>` with:\n\n- stable `id`, `parentId`, and root-to-parent `ancestorIds`;\n- `name`, `depth`, `height`, and `internal` / `external` metadata;\n- aggregate `value`;\n- `branchId`, equal to the first node below the root for that branch;\n- the direct authored `data` row, or `null` for an imputed node; and\n- direct `source` and `sourceIndexes` lineage.\n\n`branchId` is useful for inherited branch color: `color: 'branchId'` gives a\ntop-level branch and all its descendants one color without preparing a color\nfield. Paint, motion, and sort callbacks receive the same immutable node\nvalues.\n\n## Types\n\nThe exact entry exports `sunburst`, `SunburstNode`,\n`SunburstNodeComparator`, `SunburstPathOptions`, `SunburstParentOptions`, and\n`SunburstOptions`.\n\nSee [Polar Marks](./polar.md) for angular sweeps and responsive\n`PolarLength` values.\n"}
